Title: "Variadic Forms"
Id: "0017c7f2-0505-4e23-8c7b-3909a59d36cd"

Text: "A function form supports either exactly one magnetic placeholder, one or more
ordinary placeholders, or one ranged variadic mapping parameter. Mixing magnetic
and ordinary placeholders is not allowed.

```mlg-fragment
f(x__)
f(x_, y_, z_)
f(x_[i_ := 1...n])
f(x__[i_ := 1...n])
```

A magnetic placeholder `x__` lets a function-like form accept any number of
supplied arguments while the checker treats them as one tuple-like input. This
is different from `f(x_, y_, z_)`, which accepts exactly three separate
arguments.

A **ranged variadic mapping parameter** names the arity instead of hiding it:
`x_` spreads the mapping inputs while `x__` records that they are treated as a
tuple. It must be the mapping's only parameter, must bind both an index and a
length name, and must start at 0 or 1.

```mlg-fragment
Declares: f(x_[i_ := 1...n])
```

This is separate from variadic **command** arguments, which occupy a whole
`{...}` group in a command header — see Variadic Command Parameters."
Id: "2b7430b9-2dba-4332-99d3-93c71aedf31c"
